course: dictionary
lesson: 2134
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Cooler is a comparison: it means more cool, a little colder than something else. «The Little Ice Age was a cooler period in Europe.» Here cooler means the temperatures were lower than they are now.
explain: Read the words around it to pick the right meaning. A cooler can also be a box that keeps food and drinks cold on a picnic, or a machine that cools something. «Pack the juice in the cooler» means a box, not something colder. Ask which meaning fits the sentence.
explain: Slang changes the meaning again. In everyday talk, «cooler» can mean more stylish or exciting. In older films, «put in the cooler» means locked up. The context tells you which meaning the writer wants.
fact: Cooler is the comparison of cool: it means more cool, or a little colder.
fact: A cooler is a box or bag that keeps food and drinks cold, especially on picnics.
fact: A cooler can also be a machine or part that cools something, like a water cooler.
fact: «White things reflect most light, so a white T-shirt keeps you cooler in the Sun.»
fact: Slang: «cooler» can mean more stylish, and «the cooler» can mean prison, from older films.
exercise: «White things reflect most light, so a white T-shirt keeps you cooler in the Sun.» In this sentence, cooler means | *Less hot | Locked up in a cell | A box for food | More fashionable
exercise: «Pack the sandwiches and juice in the cooler for our picnic.» Here a cooler is | A prison cell | A machine that makes music | A cold wind on the hill | *A box that keeps food and drinks cold
exercise: «Some termites build mounds that keep the inside cooler than the outside.» Find and copy the word that is a comparison of cool. | inside | termites | *cooler | outside
test: «The water cooler in the school hall was broken.» What does cooler mean in this sentence? | A box for picnic food | Locked away | *A machine that cools water | More stylish
test: «In the Little Ice Age, Europe was cooler than today.» What does cooler mean here? | A box for drinks | *Colder, with lower temperatures | More fashionable | Locked away
exam: In «Tortoises from cooler places sleep through winter», cooler means | A picnic box | Stylish and exciting | *Colder places, with lower temperatures | Locked in a cell
